## Summary — one wrong justification, no design change, three small Type-3 edits

Reviewed `planning/ta-anchor-dynamic-refresh-plan.md` @ `1a116e7a` against the frozen Type 1
@ `8c2a9b04`. The refresh is a faithful and in places improved transcription — this is the only
substantive finding, and it originates in **my own Type 1 text**, not in your work.

**The `FZ-admission` decision is unchanged and correct.** The `PRC = 1` sentinel stands, the
one-replica target ceiling stands, `Reason`-tagging stands. What is wrong is the Type 1's stated
*rationale* for the ranking property, which the Type 3 transcribes as ✅ and turns into a test
assertion that cannot pass on production values.

Dean has seen this finding and confirmed the mechanism stands ("the sentinel 1 would work"),
and asked for this handoff. **No production-code change follows from it.**

Timing: the coder is at C6c and C11 is four commits out (`C6c → C6d → C6e → C6f → C11`), so
there is runway. It should land in the Type 3 before C11 is written. The trigger to the coder is
yours to send, not mine.

---

## The finding

Type 1 `planning/combined-analyzer-optimizer-design.md:1530-1533` asserts:

> **ranking** — `costEfficiency = Cost / PRC` degenerates to `Cost`, which totally orders the
> never-seen peers by cost, exactly as wanted. And because measured PRCs are ≫ 1, a never-seen
> variant ranks *behind* every measured option — conservative, and desirable: it wins only when
> nothing measured can absorb the load.

Transcribed into the Type 3 at `:1324` (§2f ranking row, marked ✅) and at `:288` (C11's four
assertions: *"ranking (it sorts **behind** every measured option)"*).

**Both halves are false, from the same root cause.** Ranking behind a measured variant needs
`Cost_s > Cost_m / P_m` — a *cost-ratio* condition. Measured PRCs being ≫ 1 is not sufficient.
And the sentinel variant's actual `Cost` is **0**:

- the anchor merge copies `Cost` from the **(a) carrier**, i.e. saturation's entry —
  `internal/engines/pipeline/analyzer_helpers.go:202`;
- saturation builds `variantCost` **only from `inputMetrics`** (live per-replica metrics) —
  `internal/engines/analyzers/saturation_v2/analyzer.go:352-360`, consumed `:373`, emitted `:443`;
- a zero-replica variant contributes no `inputMetrics`, so the map misses and `cost = 0`.

That is `N5`, and its population is *exactly* the one C11 admits. So
`costEfficiency = 0 / 1 = 0` and the sentinel sorts **first**, unconditionally — the inverse of
the stated property. Under `costGreedyRolePick` it is the **first pick** for that role.

The peer-ordering half fails too: all never-measured peers tie at `0`, and
`sortByCostEfficiencyAsc` uses unstable `sort.Slice` (`cost_aware_optimizer.go:228-235`), so the
pick among them is arbitrary, not cost-ordered.

`N5` is explicitly out of PR-2 (plan `:121`, `:2205`), so this is the **default** case, not a
corner. The plan lists `N5` and notes it reaches all three configs, but never connects it to C11.

**Why no sentinel value fixes it (and why `1` is therefore right):** `Cost = 0` makes
`costEfficiency` zero for *any* positive PRC — `1`, ε, `1e9`. The sentinel value is orthogonal to
the ranking defect. A tiny-ε variant is not an improvement; do not adopt one.

## Why the mechanism is nonetheless safe — a better argument than the Type 1 gives

Two mitigations the Type 1 does not claim, both verified at `d9f3b97e`:

1. **Self-healing after one cycle.** Once admitted with a replica, the variant has `inputMetrics`
   → real `Cost`, real PRC → normal ranking. The mis-ranking costs exactly one replica, once, per
   never-measured variant.
2. **The cap covers the non-healing case.** If that replica sticks pending (never ready → still no
   metrics → `Cost` stays 0 → picked first again), the one-replica *target* ceiling yields headroom
   0 and the variant is skipped. It cannot accumulate.

So the honest statement is: *the cap bounds it, and it self-heals in one cycle* — not *it ranks
last*. This is also why your `:2065-2080` tag/cap-coupling grep is load-bearing for correctness
rather than belt-and-braces; that paragraph is the best in the doc and should be cross-referenced
from the corrected §2f row.

---

## Requested Type-3 edits (three)

### 1. §2f ranking row (`:1324`) — ✅ → honest statement

Replace the ranking row's claim and mark it ⚠ rather than ✅. Suggested content (yours to word):

> **ranking** — `costEfficiency = Cost / PRC` degenerates to `Cost`, and for a never-measured
> variant `Cost` arrives as **0** from saturation's zero-replica path, so cost-efficiency is `0`
> and the sentinel sorts **first**, not last. No sentinel value changes this. What makes admission
> safe is the one-replica ceiling plus self-healing on the next cycle, once the variant has
> metrics — not its rank.

Please label this the way §7.1 and §2d.5 already label superseded framings, and state explicitly
that **only the Type 1's rationale is superseded, not any decision** — the mechanism and the cap
are unchanged. That keeps "the Type 1 governs" intact: no decision diverges.

**Do not edit the Type 1.** It is frozen at `8c2a9b04` and it is not your file. `:1530-1533`
needs a post-freeze touch at Dean's discretion; flag it to him rather than fixing it.

### 2. C11 assertion 2 (`:288`) — replace with a test that can pass

Current: *"ranking (it sorts **behind** every measured option)"*. That can only pass on a fixture
with a rigged non-zero `Cost`, which encodes an invariant production does not have.

Suggested replacement:

> **ranking** — a never-measured variant is selected **first** in its role, not last: its cost
> arrives as `0` from the zero-replica path, so cost-efficiency is `0`. The allocation is
> nonetheless correct — it receives **exactly one** replica and the balance goes to the cheapest
> measured variant.

Why this shape:

- **Passes on production values.** The fixture must produce `Cost = 0` the way production does —
  no replica metrics for that variant — or the spec asserts nothing.
- **Goes red on the real hazard.** Remove the cap and the sentinel absorbs the whole grant; this
  catches it. The old wording would have gone red on an unrelated cost-ratio accident.
- **Pairs with assertion 4.** Assertion 2 says the cap fires; the skip-not-zero-cap assertion says
  firing doesn't zero the model's loop.
- **Its description carries the reason.** Per §4a the spec text must name *"the saturation
  zero-replica cost bug"* in prose — no plans-branch token in the test description.

Two guard-rails to state in the same place:

- **Never assert which of several never-measured peers wins.** They tie at efficiency `0` under an
  unstable `sort.Slice` — deterministic today, not contractually. Give the fixture enough budget
  for one replica each, or assert set-level totals only.
- **Optional second spec — one cycle only.** After admission, a cycle with metrics present ranks
  the variant normally. Cheap, and it pins the self-healing property the whole design rests on.

**Optional, your call:** a *pending* spec (`PIt`) stating *"once the saturation zero-replica cost
is real, a never-measured variant ranks behind every measured option"* preserves the intended
guarantee without encoding a false invariant or carrying a red test; whoever fixes that bug flips
it on. Skip it if you'd rather not carry a dormant spec.

### 3. Two additions to the C11 grep/notes block (`:2065-2080`)

- **Which path the specs run through.** Eligibility and ranking must be exercised through the
  **cost** optimizer. `fairShareRolePick` additionally gates on `available[vc.AcceleratorName]`
  (`greedy_score_optimizer.go:419-422`) against a map keyed by real accelerator types
  (`mergeConstraints`, `cost_aware_optimizer.go:327-349`); a never-measured variant's
  `AcceleratorName` is **empty** from the same zero-replica lookup
  (`saturation_v2/analyzer.go:372`, filled from `replicas[0]` only when replicas exist at
  `:417-418`), so `available[""] = 0` and it is skipped there **regardless of PRC**.
  `costGreedyRolePick` ignores the `available` map entirely (parameter `_`,
  `cost_aware_optimizer.go:85-109`), so the sentinel is eligible on that path.
  **This is pre-existing and must NOT be fixed inside C11** — but without the note the coder
  debugs a working sentinel for an afternoon. I find no existing label for this half; `N5` covers
  only the `Cost` half.
- **The comment C11 invalidates.** `analyzer_helpers.go:213-216` currently reads *"Not proactively
  selectable; genuine cold-starts fall to the reactive scale-from-zero engine"* — the exact claim
  C11 reverses. Your grep list catches the new `Reason` constant and the literal `1` but not this.

